    "show_share": true,
    "description": "In the early hours of the morning in the Cardiac Intensive Care Unit, CICU, a mother worries about her sleeping child's raspy, irregular breathing. She looks at the machine he's hooked up to - a machine that monitors his heartbeat - to make sure he's doing okay. It doesn't allay her fears and she counts the hours till a nurse comes in and provides her with an update about her child's progress. He's stable, she's relieved but only momentarily. That's because her son may never have a carefree childhood since he would require constant follow-ups throughout his life.",
